@startuml cli-workflow
' The canonical operator workflow: inspect a corpus, train the two experts
' independently, assemble them into a hybrid, evaluate, then serve. The key fact
' the diagram encodes is that `train hybrid` consumes two ALREADY-TRAINED model
' files - it never reads a corpus - so the two training arms are independent and
' may be run in parallel or reused across several hybrids.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/cli-workflow.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/cli/README.md §4 and Figure 1 in
' docs/training/hybrid.md §2.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title grammstein — End-to-End Operator Workflow

rectangle "**Corpus**\nplaintext · wikipedia · gutenberg" as corpus #455A64
rectangle "**corpus stats / detect / sample**\nsize · language · spot-check" as inspect #546E7A

rectangle "**train ngram**\n⟨CORPUS⟩ ⟨OUTPUT⟩\n""--order 5"" · ""--min-count 2""" as tngram #1565C0
rectangle "**train embedding**\n⟨CORPUS⟩ ⟨OUTPUT⟩\n""--dim 100"" · ""--epochs 5""" as tembed #2E7D32

rectangle "**ngram.bin**\nMKN n-gram model" as mngram #1565C0
rectangle "**embed.bin**\nsubword embedding" as membed #2E7D32

rectangle "**train hybrid**\n⟨NGRAM_MODEL⟩ ⟨EMBEDDING_MODEL⟩ ⟨OUTPUT⟩\n""--strategy"" · ""--alpha 0.8""\n**reads no corpus**" as thybrid #1B6CA8
rectangle "**hybrid.bin**" as mhybrid #1B6CA8

rectangle "**eval perplexity**\n**eval compare**" as evaluate #546E7A
rectangle "**convert to-static**\nDoubleArrayTrie — faster reads" as static #00838F
rectangle "**query** score · similar · completions\n**repl**" as serve #546E7A

corpus --> inspect
inspect --> tngram
inspect --> tembed
corpus --> tngram
corpus --> tembed

tngram --> mngram
tembed --> membed

mngram --> thybrid : NGRAM_MODEL
membed --> thybrid : EMBEDDING_MODEL
thybrid --> mhybrid

mhybrid --> evaluate
mngram ..> evaluate : n-gram models\nevaluate too
evaluate --> serve : keep the lowest\nheld-out perplexity
mhybrid --> static
static --> serve

@enduml
